# civil-holidays v1
# jurisdiction: EG
# source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_holidays_in_Egypt
#   (the statutory list; Islamic dates resolve through the tabular Islamic
#   calendar). Cross-checked against vacanza/holidays 0.101 (MIT). Names are the
#   official Arabic.
#
#   ISLAMIC DATES ARE TABULATED: chronologia resolves the Islamic holidays
#   through the arithmetic tabular Hijri calendar (islamic_civil, basis
#   "tabulated"), an honest deterministic model. Egypt's actual observance and
#   the reference's estimates are astronomical/decreed and can differ by ±1-2
#   days; those differences (plus Egypt's "يوم تعويضي" compensatory-day shifts,
#   which are NOT modelled) are catalogued as documented disagreements in the
#   differential test, not smoothed over. Sham Ennessim (شم النسيم) is the
#   Monday after Coptic (Orthodox) Easter, an Easter offset on the
#   Julian-Gregorian reckoning.
# retrieved: 2026-07-22
# categories: public|regional|municipal|religious|school
# columns: kind | name | args | categories | subdiv | observed | valid | span
#
# --- fixed civil / Coptic ---
fixed  | عيد الميلاد المجيد                | 1 7   | public religious |  |
